SUMMARY: Lessons of Light and Water by Dawn Adams
DESCRIPTION:Lessons of Light and Water by Dawn Adams explores the healing
  power of the natural world through paintings inspired by water and sky. 
 This body of work reflects the artist's personal journey through grief wh
 ile offering viewers a space for reflection and renewal.\n\nWater and sky
  serve as powerful subjects throughout the exhibition\, evoking both emot
 ional and psychological responses. They invite contemplation while sugges
 ting themes of transformation\, peace\, and the unknown.\n\nUsing layered
  oil paint and a combination of traditional and unconventional techniques
 \, Adams creates richly textured works filled with depth\, atmosphere\, a
 nd light. Her paintings celebrate nature's ability to comfort\, inspire\,
  and heal.\n\nView Lessons of Light and Water at Pillar Arts By Hand Gall
 ery from May 1 through June 26. Visitors are also invited to meet the art
 ist during Gallery Walk receptions on Friday\, May 1 and Friday\, June 5 
 from 5–8 PM.
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Exhibition,Free,Gallery,In-Person,Visual-Arts
