SUMMARY: FACES: Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, live music by Illica Pozz
 atti.
DESCRIPTION:Paintings\, prints\, drawings\, live music by Illica Pozzatti
 .\n\nIllica Pozzatti is a Bloomington-based visual artist and musician wh
 ose career is defined by a lifelong immersion in the arts. Raised in Indi
 ana as the youngest of five\, her background was steeped in creative expr
 ession from the very beginning\; she first picked up a paintbrush by age 
 3 and began piano lessons at 5. Named after the famed librettist Luigi Il
 lica\, she was deeply influenced by her father\, the renowned printmaker 
 and painter Rudy Pozzatti. From him\, she inherited not only technical sk
 ill but a profound understanding of the patience and keen observation req
 uired to navigate the modern art world.\n\nAfter earning two degrees from
  Indiana University\, Illica’s professional journey took her from an art 
 director role at Hirons Advertising to the Guggenheim Museum in New York 
 City. While in NYC\, her musical roots flourished as she took up guitar a
 nd voice lessons\, eventually leading to the 2012 release of her record\,
  Queens & Kings\, produced by David Bianco in Hollywood.\n\nAs a visual a
 rtist\, Illica focuses primarily on representational painting and drawing
 . Her work often centers on the human figure\, seeking to peel back layer
 s of color and form to reveal deeper psychological aspects of her subject
 s. Guided by the belief that imagination is the essential element of any 
 "skillful invention\," she finds particular joy in the collaborative natu
 re of commissions. Today\, Illica serves as the founder of the H&B appare
 l brand (Haute & Bothered)\, a lifestyle label where she seamlessly blend
 s her expertise in fine arts and graphic design with her passion for musi
 c. Whether she is designing local apparel or planning her next record\, h
 er diverse creative projects can be found at http://www.IllicaSandbox.com
 .
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Exhibition,Gallery,Free
