SUMMARY: Godzilla Weekend: Mothra Madness - FILM FESTIVAL
DESCRIPTION:BCT’s 2nd annual Godzilla Weekend is showcasing this giant mo
 th that attacks the whole world with fury!\n\n\nDAY TWO will feature thre
 e essential Godzilla films along. Presented by The East Asian Studies Cen
 ter https://easc.indiana.edu/index.html \, The Media School https://media
 school.indiana.edu/index.html \, Tattoo Ka https://www.tattookaiju.com/ i
 ju https://www.tattookaiju.com/ \, and Buskirk-Chumley Theater.\n\nTalks\
 , vendors\, and additional Godzilla fun and performances in between!\n\nD
 oors open at 11AM !\n\n\nMothra vs. Godzilla (Ishiro Honda\, 1964) 12PM –
  1:30PM\n\nGodzilla faces off against the benevolent insect monster-god M
 othra in this clash of the titans\, a crossover battle between two of Toh
 o Studios’ most popular monsters—the last in which Godzilla would figure 
 as a malevolent villain rather than a fearsome hero. Mothra vs. Godzilla 
 marks a creative high point in the Godzilla series\, with pointed social 
 commentary from director Ishiro Honda\, a masterful score by Akira Ifukub
 e\, and astonishing special-effects work by Eiji Tsuburaya.\n\nDCP Format
 \nSubtitled\nNot Rated\n1hr 29mins\n\nDestroy All Monsters (Ishiro Honda\
 , 1968) 2:15PM – 3:45PM\nThe original Godzilla team of director Ishiro Ho
 nda\, special-effects supervisor Eiji Tsuburaya\, and composer Akira Ifuk
 ube reunited for this kaiju extravaganza\, which features no fewer than e
 leven monsters. Set in the remote future of 1999\, when the people of Ear
 th have achieved world peace by confining destructive creatures to Monste
 rland (until an alien race intervenes)\, Destroy All Monsters mounts a th
 rilling display of innovative action sequences and memorable images that 
 have made it a favorite for generations of viewers.\n\nDCP Format\nSubtit
 led\nNot Rated\n1hr 29mins\n\nGodzilla\, Mothra\, and King Ghidorah: Gian
 t Monsters All Out Attack (Shusuke Kaneko 2001) 4:30PM – 6:15PM\n\nIn thi
 s brand-new adventure\, Godzilla returns to his “bad guy” roots as he ram
 pages through Japan just like in the good ol’ days. In response\, an anci
 ent religious sect resurrects the legendary “Holy Beasts of Yamato” (Ghid
 orah\, Mothra and Baragon) to protect Japan and destroy the threat of God
 zilla forever.\n\nDCP Format\nSubtitled\nNot Rated\n1hr 45mins
CATEGORIES:Bloomington,Film,In-Person,Tickets
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62fb9509b27fd5
 06428328ed/69e8eed95f82b9dab7838f53/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:BCT’s 2nd annual Godzilla Weekend is showcasing this
  giant moth that attacks the whole world with fury! DAY TWO will feature 
 three essential Godzilla films...
